<BaseLayout title="About the game" description="Project Gotthard is an independent science-fiction command and management game. Lead a classified European programme in an alternate 1994.">
<div class="container page-content"><header class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Programme briefing / 01</p><h1>You give the orders.<br />The unknown answers.</h1><p class="lead">A science-fiction command and management game set in an alternate October 1994.</p></header><div class="prose"><h2>Beneath the Alps</h2><p>A classified European military programme has opened the way to worlds beyond Earth. From an underground Alpine facility, you take responsibility for the people and decisions that shape what comes next.</p><h2>The commander's role</h2><p>The intended experience centres on running the programme: recruiting and preparing teams, organising expeditions, responding to reports, and balancing research, diplomacy and security. You command the effort rather than directly controlling soldiers in the field.</p><p>Information is part of the challenge. A report describes what was observed; it cannot tell you everything that is happening. Preparation and judgement matter when events develop beyond your immediate view.</p><h2>A place and a period</h2><p>The setting brings together an alternate European 1994, Alpine military engineering and the uneasy promise of exploration. The programme begins in a world of physical workspaces, reports and human responsibility.</p><h2>Development status</h2><p>Project Gotthard is in development. This site introduces its vision and records the process. Features described here express the intended experience; each future development report will distinguish implemented work, experiments and plans.</p><p>There is no public release date or download announced here. Follow <a href={path('devlog/')}>The Gotthard Files</a> for reviewed updates.</p><h2>Questions from outside the mountain</h2><h3>Is this an original game?</h3><p>Yes. Project Gotthard is an independent, original science-fiction project with its own setting and identity. It is not affiliated with an existing television or film franchise.</p><h3>Which platforms will it support?</h3><p>Public platform and system requirements will be shared when they are ready to be confirmed.</p><h3>Where can I follow development?</h3><p>Read the journal or subscribe to the <a href={path('rss.xml')}>RSS feed</a>. Official community and storefront destinations will be added when available.</p></div></div>
</BaseLayout>
